{"ld": 239, "paper": "SP105", "session": "132", "title": "An Act to Allow Retail Pharmacies to Operate Remote Dispensing Sites in Rural Areas", "sponsor_id": "s-farrin-bradlee", "cosponsor_ids": ["h-arford-poppy", "s-beebe-center-anne", "h-cloutier-kristen", "h-salisbury-suzanne"], "committee_code": "HCIFS", "committee_name": "Health Coverage, Insurance and Financial Services", "summary": {"text": "This bill directs the Maine Board of Pharmacy to establish the terms and conditions for the operation and licensing of a remote dispensing site by a retail pharmacy by rule. The bill requires that the rules establish terms and conditions that, at a minimum, include a demonstration that the geographic area in which the remote dispensing site is to be located lacks adequate access to retail pharmacy services for the general public; requirements for the use of a remote dispensing site that allows for storage, preparation, packaging, labeling and dispensing of prescription drugs and remote oversight by a licensed pharmacist; and requirements for minimum staffing, compliance with federal and state pharmacy laws, record keeping and security.\n\nThe bill provides that a remote dispensing site may not be operated until rules are adopted by the board.", "official": true, "source": "Bill text, https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0105&item=1&snum=132"}, "status": "enacted", "status_label": "Enacted", "final_disposition": {"label": "Enacted", "date": "2025-05-29", "governor_action": "Signed", "governor_action_date": "2025-05-29"}, "fiscal_status": "Not Yet Determined", "documents": [{"label": "Bill text (LD 239)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0105&item=1&snum=132", "item": 1}, {"label": "Amendment C-A (S-85)", "url": "https://legislature.maine.gov/legis/bills/getPDF.asp?paper=SP0105&item=2&snum=132", "item": 2}], "amendments": [{"id": "C-A (S-85)", "description": null, "sponsor": null, "status": "Adopted by House & Sena